# Line endings are OS-independent by decree, not by each contributor's git
# config.  Without this file the working-tree EOL depends on `core.autocrlf`,
# an ambient per-machine setting — so a Windows checkout gets CRLF, and any
# test comparing a committed file byte-for-byte against a freshly generated
# string (doc/manpage consistency, the diagnostics scan) fails there while
# passing on Linux.  `encoding="utf-8"` does NOT fix this: encoding and line
# ending are orthogonal.  Force LF in every working tree on every OS.
#
# The 2026-09-12 Windows CI break was the same disease one level up: a byte
# offset shifted 531 -> 540 because 9 LF newlines became CRLF at checkout.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never normalised, never EOL-touched.  `text=auto` already
# auto-detects these, but declaring them removes the guess.
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.7z   binary
*.TTC  binary
